# `make shim` puts the built libraries here, one per architecture, and the binary embeds them:
#
#   i2cshim-linux-amd64.so
#   i2cshim-linux-arm64.so
#
# They are built by shim/build.sh into shim/build/ and copied in. The directory is committed empty
# so the embed pattern in ../shim.go always matches something: a build without the libraries is
# fine, and a node that needs one says so when it starts.
